<title>SOUTH KOREA: Ssangyong wins $225 mln Singapore building order.</title>
<headline>Ssangyong wins $225 mln Singapore building order.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Ssangyong Engineering and Construction Co Ltd, an unlisted unit of Ssangyong Group, said on Thursday it has won a $225 million order to build a high rise building in Singapore. </p>
<p>Ssangyong said in a statement that the order was awarded by Posbank Center Pte Ltd.</p>
<p>The construction of the 52-storey building in Singapore's financial district is scheduled to be completed by early 2000, it said.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
